    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can you summarize the specific steps our company needs to follow when we receive a formal \"Right to be Forgotten\" request from a user, according to GDPR guidelines? We need to make sure we aren't missing any technical or administrative requirements for complete data erasure.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Upon receiving a formal GDPR \"Right to be Forgotten\" request, your company must first verify the identity of the user and confirm the request's legality before launching the data deletion process. Administratively, you are obligated to delete or anonymize the individual's personal data across all storage systems, including backups, while simultaneously notifying any third parties the data was shared with so they can also erase their copies. Technically, this requires implementing secure deletion methods that render data irrecoverable, ensuring that metadata and caching systems do not inadvertently retain traces. Finally, maintain detailed records of this processing decision for at least three years as required by regulatory audits, even if the data itself is no longer accessible.",
